# UI opening and closing transitions

- When creating or editing an expandable section, menu, drawer or dialog, implement a visible transition in both directions. An opening-only animation is incomplete.
- Start closing motion before applying `hidden`, closing/removing the element or retiring its layout space. Preserve final layout without a snap and move related headings/dividers with their content.
- Reuse the approved motion language and existing transition helpers. Honor explicit requests for instant actions and reduced-motion settings.
- Keep interactions reversible under rapid clicks, clean up interrupted animations on navigation/context changes and preserve focus, `aria-expanded`, inert state and keyboard access.
- Animate presentation without delaying task persistence. Verify opening, closing, interruption, responsive bounds and reduced motion in a real browser.
- Website edits do not authorize updating the frozen native bundle; follow the mobile release gate.
